#
# - TF_GLM_PROMPT_PARTIALS=fp32|bf16 (default fp32 on every TP; opt-in, with TF_GLM_HC_SPLIT=1). bf16: each rank's
#   partial of the peers' rows goes out as bf16 (p2p; staged in the all-gather buffer's unused part, also in a
#   micro-batch half's region), and every rank's partial of a row is rounded to bf16 before the sum, which stays in fp32
#   rank 0 first, then rounded to bf16 as before; the owner rounds its own partial as the others round theirs. An
#   unsplit chunk (shorter than TF_GLM_HC_SPLIT_MIN_ROWS) and the all-gather exchange round the same way in hc_post
#   (glue.hc_post / hc_post_pair / hc_post_ranks: round_parts; the kernel takes fp32 or bf16 partials), so a row's bits
#   do not depend on the chunking, the exchange, the own-row front or the micro-batches. Decode windows, verify and the
#   MTP head keep fp32 partials. The setting is in the ranks' startup comparison (SplitSettings.code).
# - TF_NCCL_RING_INPLACE (default 1, with TF_NCCL_RING=1): the ring exchange's link all-gathers run in place (a rank
#   packs what it sends into its own slot of the link's output, nothing zero-filled), each link's steps on its own
#   stream, joined to the other link's only where relayed bytes pass; 0 keeps 0098's pack / all-gather / unpack steps.
#   The same bytes arrive either way (0098's exchange is the same design as the GLM-5.3 recipe's 0142).
